// ROOFS by style name. The model picks a style and a few options; the tool builds a skilled roof: correct stair
// facing, half and corner shapes at hips and valleys, closed steep faces, gable walls, verges, eaves (plain, flared,
// cornice with dentils), ridge caps or crests, dormers, a classical pediment, chimneys and a tower, over a rectangle or
// a union of rectangles (L, T, U plans). Under the roof stays hollow (an attic).
//
//   roof(g, footprint, style, opts)   footprint: [x0,z0,x1,z1] | [[x0,z0,x1,z1], ...] | {from,to}; opts.y = eave course
